-- Aggregate Functions

-- Aggregate functions in SQL are used to perform calculations on multiple rows of data and return one single result.

-- | Function | Purpose                      | Syntax             |
-- | -------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------|
-- | COUNT()  | Counts the number of records | COUNT(Column_Name) |
-- | SUM()    | Calculates the total         | SUM(Column_Name)   |
-- | AVG()    | Calculates the average       | AVG(Column_Name)   |
-- | MIN()    | Finds the minimum value      | MIN(Column_Name)   |
-- | MAX()    | Finds the maximum value      | MAX(Column_Name)   |

